-- הודעת תכ"ם HOD.13.4.7.1 — סכום לתשלום החזר הוצאות טלפון קווי אישי בהתאם לרמת זכאות (גרסה 2, 1.1.2018)
-- The notice's second edition, issued with the second edition of
-- instruction H.13.4.7 after the refund was cancelled from 1.3.2017 for all
-- but a few gradings. It prints the same two tables as the first edition,
-- now citing the level as set in the instruction's annex B. Its own figures
-- are kept here as its own data; the levels and the standing (existing or
-- new) are the types of the first edition's file, which this one imports.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `2008-12-01_takam_HOD-13-4-7-1_telefon-ramot-zakaut_v1`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ is ‘בעל תפקיד’, the
-- holder of a post, not a husband; the notice prices a refund of phone
-- expenses by entitlement level and makes no distinction by sex.

§ `סכום לתשלום החזר הוצאות טלפון קווי אישי בהתאם לרמת זכאות (גרסה 2)`

§§ `1`

-- §1 and its table: the monthly sum for an existing role holder, by the
-- level set for him in annex B of instruction 13.4.7: 100.8, 139.2, 196.8
-- and 235.5 shekels for levels א to ד.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1/t1
GIVEN l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 2` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `landline level A` THEN 100.8
    WHEN `landline level B` THEN 139.2
    WHEN `landline level C` THEN 196.8
    WHEN `landline level D` THEN 235.5

§§ `2`

-- §2 (its subsection printed "1.2") and its table: the monthly sum for a
-- new role holder, 96 shekels at level א and 144 at level ב; no level ג or
-- ד, which annex B gives a new holder neither.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2 akn:hc_1__para_1-2 akn:hc_1__para_1-2/t1
GIVEN l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 2` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `landline level A` THEN JUST 96
    WHEN `landline level B` THEN JUST 144
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The two tables as one answer, NOTHING where they print no sum.
GIVEN s IS A `landline role-holder standing`
      l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 2` s l IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `an existing landline role holder` THEN JUST (`the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 2` l)
    WHEN `a new landline role holder` THEN `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 2` l

§§ `Worked examples`

#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 2` `an existing landline role holder` `landline level C` EQUALS JUST 196.8
#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 2` `a new landline role holder` `landline level B` EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT isNothing (`the monthly landline sum under notice edition 2` `a new landline role holder` `landline level D`)

-- The second edition changed none of the first edition's sums: for every
-- standing and level the two tables give the same answer.
`the landline sums of 2018 are those of 2008` MEANS
    all (GIVEN s YIELD
            all (GIVEN l YIELD
                    `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 2` s l
                        EQUALS `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` s l)
                (LIST `landline level A`, `landline level B`, `landline level C`, `landline level D`))
        (LIST `an existing landline role holder`, `a new landline role holder`)
#ASSERT `the landline sums of 2018 are those of 2008`
